Do not take an echo the filters no longer explain for the near end's talk

When the echo path changes in a call (another output, an echo 30 ms nearer or
farther), the filters no longer fit it and the refined filter adds energy instead
of removing it, while the residual echo estimate, scaled by an ERLE learnt before
the change, falls far below the echo left in the near end signal. The dominant
near end detector then takes that echo for the near end's talk, the suppressor
goes transparent for some 300 ms, and the echo goes through. With patch 0019 the
echo of 2 ms is cancelled well (ERLE some 17 dB, where main does not reach it),
so after a change to 30 ms this happened more often than with main.

The suppressor now gets whether the refined filter adds energy on all capture
channels. When it does and the linear echo estimate says more echo than the near
end holds in the detector's bands (1 to 15), in a share of the latest blocks of
0.15 or more (a mean with a rate of 1/16; three such blocks in a row), the
detector is fed the near end as the echo, which neither starts nor ends its
near end state. In double talk this comes in single blocks and changes nothing.

Tried and dropped: holding the detector for 50 blocks once both filters diverge
(words -0.85 dB); a correlation gate between the error and the echo estimate
(words -0.26 to -0.57 dB); ending the near end state at once on such blocks
(words -0.13 to -0.41 dB); the same gate without the share (words -0.06 dB).

Simulator (AEC3 alone, 16 kHz, headroom 512, speech-like ends, room responses,
the same seeds), against this branch with 0019 and against main:
- a change of output in a call, 30 to 2 ms and back (72 runs): runs with 1 dB or
  more of echo than main 14 before, 6 now (main against itself with dither: 9);
  echo 3.9 dB below main on average (before 0.3); 22 runs with less echo than
  before, none with more; words unchanged;
- a change in a call, 2 to 180 ms (54 runs): 11 runs with less echo, none more;
- a change between a short and a long echo (60/10, 50/5, 40/8, 100/10 ms both
  ways, 96 runs): 3 runs with less echo, none more;
- unmute after a change of output, short echo (192 and 96 runs), normal delays
  (84 runs), unmute grids: echo unchanged; of over 9,000 words, 2 lose 3 dB or
  more (both at an echo of -6 dB, in double talk right after the restart), no
  other word moves by 1 dB.
Unit tests: the near end is found while the refined filter adds no energy; an
echo the filters no longer explain, block after block, is not taken for it;
single such blocks leave the detection as it is; it comes back afterwards.

